20. polaris-backend is the gradle repo matching the hook's squawk path, last reflog 13:44:37 on main; jcmd present in OOM dump = gradle/java running
21. PROOF 1 (capped test repo): single "git add" re-entered post-index-change 5 levels, stopped only by artificial cap
22. PROOF 2: read-only git commands (status/diff/ls-files/rev-parse) do NOT fire the hook -> trigger was a real index write
23. PROOF 3: hook doing "git stash push -k -u" produced 70 stashes from ONE git add, while depth guard still read depth=1
    -> git stash push spawns fresh hook processes that do not inherit an env-var guard, so recursion is uncontainable that way
24. PROOF 4: reference-transaction fires twice per ref update (prepared/committed) and is symlinked to the same _chain
    -> second independent bomb: stash push creates refs -> reference-transaction -> _chain -> stash push -> ...
25. VERDICT: global core.hooksPath symlinks post-index-change AND reference-transaction to a pre-commit script that mutates
    the index and refs. Unbounded git fork storm, ~24500 processes, 28.5GB anon + 8GB swap exhausted, OOM killer picked a
    5MB victim (code-tunnel, oom_score_adj 200) which freed nothing, machine wedged, hard reset at 14:26:22.
